@startuml frame_loop_sequence
title Frame loop: a variable frame rate driving the fixed 1 kHz simulation through the session
autonumber
participant "Front end\n(later the Godot binding)" as Frontend
participant "session::Session" as Session
participant "FixedStepClock" as Clock
participant "controls::pro / easy" as Controls
participant "run::step" as Run

note over Frontend : The front end owns the device input and measures\nthe frame time. The core never reads time or devices.

Frontend -> Session : create(Setup)
Session --> Frontend : optional<Session>

loop every rendered frame
  Frontend -> Session : advance(Controls, elapsed_ns)
  Session -> Clock : advance(elapsed_ns)
  Clock --> Session : Advance {steps, dropped_ns}\n(steps <= max_steps_per_frame)
  loop steps times (until the run has a result)
    Session -> Controls : the layout's input from Controls\n(easy: the assist reads the engine and gear)
    Controls --> Session : vehicle::Input
    Session -> Run : step(state, model, rules, input, dt_s = 0.001)
    Run --> Session : pull::Output
    note right of Session : snapshots are taken before\nand after the last step only
  end
  Session --> Frontend : Frame {steps, dropped_ns}
  Frontend -> Session : previous(), current(), alpha()
  Frontend -> Frontend : draw blend(previous, current, alpha)
  opt result()
    Frontend -> Frontend : show the result; after a full pull,\na new Session on sled::heavier()
  end
end
@enduml
